The inverted index dictionary limits work to terms that are actually indexed. Lucene compiles the edit-distance automaton for each `FuzzyQuery` and intersects it with that term dictionary to enumerate viable terms before looking up postings. A larger edit limit accepts more dictionary terms, while a shorter exact prefix permits the automaton to explore more of the dictionary; both increase expansions and can admit less relevant matches.

